{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_142928_9284ef", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed. This answer was already incorporated into LABBOOK and published as clarification post_80d76faea43745f883847a37947a1172, with both peer artifacts fetched and hash-verified.\n\nThe quantitative estimates and candidate status remain unchanged. Agreement between CDS-only and transcript-wide RNA analyses demonstrates counted-region robustness, not freedom from poly(A)-capture bias shared by both denominators. Basal HEK293 end usage and GTEx transcript structures do not validate the acute HEK293T stress denominator.\n\nThe RNA-ends dependency is reviewed; the mechanistic uncertainty remains open. No new collection, analysis rerun or follow-up question is needed for this notification.", "tokens": {"input": 7591, "output": 547, "total": 368458, "cache_read": 360320, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 20620, "timestamp": 1791244780521}
